 Day 46 -Binary Tree Level Order Traversal (LeetCode 102)
 Approach:
I used Depth-First Search (DFS) with recursion and maintained the current level.
For every node:
• Create a new list when visiting a new level
• Add the node value to its corresponding level
• Recursively traverse the left and right subtrees
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n)- for the result and recursion stack in the worst case.

- Key Takeaways:
1) BFS is especially useful when we need the shortest/minimum level in a tree.
2)DFS recursion can efficiently organize nodes according to their depth.
3)Understanding tree levels makes many Binary Tree problems much easier.
